hooks/sandbox-allow.log
*.log
node_modules
**/__pycache__
# real config values, UNTRACKED since the Octopus "Claude Harness" library variable set
# became the cross-machine source of truth (scripts/octopus-config-sync.sh fetch|push).
# The example file stays tracked as the schema; install.ps1 seeds a fresh clone from it.
/harness-config.json
# per-machine repo roots + discovered slug->path index (PROJ-15143) -- lives at
# ~/.claude/.harness-local.json, outside this repo's tree; defensive entry only, in
# case it's ever relocated under skills/ or hooks/
.harness-local.json
# real chat-log transcripts, centralized here via reversed symlinks (session cwd holds
# a symlink pointing in here) -- never publish real conversation content in a repo other
# adopters clone.
/Chat files/
# reversed symlinks in the repo root pointing into /Chat files/ -- per-machine,
# hardcode an absolute local path, dangle on any other clone. The /Chat files/ entry
# above only covers the central directory, not this half of the design.
/*Chat.md
# per-machine session bookkeeping (real files here now, symlinked back from
# ~/.claude/sessions.txt|.md via scripts/install.ps1) -- adopter-specific runtime
# state, never shareable.
/sessions.txt
/sessions.md
# never commit a private key/cert, or a plaintext-secret scratch file like the one this
# repo briefly had at "MongoDb connection for cohorts and cohort reports/" -- see
# ama-mongo-access skill, connection strings get pulled live from ECS, never stored here.
*.pem
/MongoDb connection for cohorts and cohort reports/
